𐤉 (ʾš ly /⁠ʔas lī⁠/, “my”). These were derived from the relative pronoun *ʔas or prefix *-ʔas in combination with the dative prefix *-l, hence the Hebrew is equivalent to ש־ (she, “which”) + ל־ (l, “to”), thus “which [belongs] to”. The first use of של as a possessive marker in Hebrew is attested in late parts of the Hebrew Bible, but then still preceded by, and in addition to, a possessive suffix (cf. Canticles 1:6; 3:7). In Mishnaic Hebrew, של־ (…","tpl":[{"k":20,"lang":146,"form":"𐤔𐤋𐤉","gloss":"my"},{"k":20,"lang":84,"form":"𐤀𐤔 𐤋𐤉","gloss":"my"},{"k":79,"lang":"he","form":"ש־ + ל־"}]},"rel":{"d":["סוּג שֶׁל"]}},{"w":"של־","p":"ADP","s":[{"g":"alternative form of שֶׁל (shel); not used predicatively","t":69}],"f":[["שֶׁלְּ־",13],["shel'-",0]],"ety":{"text":"From שֶׁ־ (she-, “that, which”) + לְ־ (l'-, “to”). Attested since Mishnaic Hebrew. More recently supplanted by the standalone form שֶׁל (shél), but the inflected forms are unchanged.","tpl":[]}}],"שלחו":[{"w":"שלחו","p":"VERB","s":[{"g":"(nonstandard form) Third-person plural past (suffix conjugation) of שִׁלַּח (shilách).","t":82,"x":["שִׁלְחוּ בָאֵשׁ מִקְדָּשֶׁךָ"]}]}],"תבל":[{"w":"תבל","p":"NOUN","s":[{"g":"world, universe","t":98}],"f":[["תֵּבֵל",17],["tevél",0]],"ipa":[{"i":"/teˈvel/","t":14}],"rel":{"d":["שִׁבְעַת פִּלְאֵי תֵּבֵל"]}},{"w":"תבל","p":"NOUN","s":[{"g":"abomination, perversion","t":65},{"g":"spice, seasoning"}],"f":[["קֶטֶל",21],["תֶּבֶל",15],["tével",0]],"ipa":[{"i":"/ˈtevel/","t":14}],"rel":{"r":["תַּבְלִין"]}},{"w":"תבל","p":"VERB","s":[{"g":"defective spelling of תיבל.","t":58}],"f":[["תִּבֵּל",13],["tibél",0]]},{"w":"תבל","p":"VERB","s":[{"g":"defective spelling of תובל.","t":71}],"f":[["תֻּבַּל",13],["tubál",0]]},{"w":"תבל","p":"PROPN","s":[{"g":"Tabal (a region of Asia Minor, roughly equivalent to Cappadocia).","x":["יָוָן תֻּבַל וָמֶשֶׁךְ הֵמָּה רֹכְלָיִךְ בְּנֶפֶשׁ אָדָם וּכְלֵי נְחֹשֶׁת נָתְנוּ מַעֲרָבֵךְ׃"]},{"g":"A \"son\" of Japheth.","x":["בְּנֵי יֶפֶת גֹּמֶר וּמָגוֹג וּמָדַי וְיָ